  "title": "What a write-ahead log solves, and what it costs",
  "summary": "A write-ahead log replaces a scatter of page flushes at commit time with one sequential append and one flush, which is why commits survive power cuts. The price is duplicated writes, a flush on the commit path, and checkpointing that costs disk space and recovery time.",
